# Explicit per-record mathematical dispositions; no metadata-only novelty claims.
notes={
323195:('parked_structural_order_problem','Conjecture 6.3 in Section 6. Underlying group is already known; must identify the positive cone, not recompute K0 as a group. One-relator cases checked by the author do not settle all finitely separated graphs.','Need a positive K0 class outside the graph cone, or a full positive-cone surjectivity argument. No finite certificate route identified.','Source v1/v2 Section 6 conjectures and examples inspected; later citing-body audit incomplete.'),
323253:('parked_homology_torsion','Conjecture 1.6 is an iff assertion about both existence of order-three elements and elementary entire homology. Proposition 1.4 already covers r>=3 for existence and the nonvanishing 3-group range; proving only these is duplication.','Unproved r=2 general existence and elementary exponent-three classification; cannot substitute mod-3 Betti numbers for integral torsion. Huge boundary matrices make unguided execution inappropriate.','Source v1/v2 parameter translation, Proposition 1.4 and Conjecture 1.6 inspected; no Smith-normal-form computation.'),
323424:('parked_geometric_homology','Source Definition 1.1 is admissible orthogonal subspace decorations of colored planar trivalent graphs. Proposition 1.3 computes a projective-bundle example with even homology. Its failure of the MOY Poincare-polynomial hypothesis is NOT failure of odd-homology vanishing. Grant 1212.4511 Remark 6.4 still assumes even homology.','Need a full even-cell or spectral-sequence degeneration argument through all MOY moves, or an actual odd cycle with certified nonboundary in an admissible source moduli space. Graph labels alone do not define that space.','Source Definition 1.1, Proposition 1.3 proof, Conjecture 1.6; Grant relevant remark/body read. Full topology literature incomplete.'),
323533:('excluded_known_resolution_and_source_formula','Source Conjecture 6.1 is the truncated Jacobi product coefficient inequality. Wang 2108.04148 introduction identifies independent Mao and Yee proofs in 2015 and later positive-series identities. Exponents match R*j*(j+1)/2-S*j and that plus (2j+1)S.','No new target remains in reproducing these known proofs; strictness needs exact coefficient comparison if documenting status, not new credit.','Source both versions; later Wang introduction and displayed positive series inspected. Original Mao/Yee bodies not independently acquired, so not claiming comprehensive proof audit.'),
323558:('excluded_source_own_refutation','Mollard Section 3 states the exact conjecture then disproves it using already published C4 product formula. For k=3,n=4, his formula gives 9+ceil(10/2)=14 rather than 15. This is printed source reasoning, not a new finite counterexample.','None for a new discovery; do not formalize this as new credit.','Complete short source conjecture/refutation passage and construction section read. No witness search.'),
323592:('excluded_source_own_theorem','Source Theorem 3.1 already supplies exactly the central-monomial basis and homogeneous R/F and L/E components. Its proof invokes the diamond lemma then checks degree multiplication. The generalized phi was already arbitrary in source Definition 2.3.','No new endpoint. Missing commutation/q hypotheses in a shortened database rendering are not permission for a degenerate reinterpretation.','Source Definition 2.3 and full Theorem 3.1 proof read.'),
323732:('parked_hard_graph_representation','The inclusion from bounded tolerance to tolerance+cocomparability is known. Source main theorem handles a representation with one unbounded vertex; it does not cover arbitrary representations.','Need a genuinely general representation-normalization lemma or a graph with explicit tolerance and cocomparability certificates plus impossibility of every bounded representation. Enumerating one failed drawing is insufficient.','Primary introduction/main range inspected; full 58-page technical proof and later citing works not completely read.'),
323748:('parked_radical_rigidity','Conjecture 9.4 equates quadratic solvability, radical solvability and recursively defined F. Planar theorem is already proved. The source reduces it to a three-connected characterization, so gluing planar pieces alone cannot remove the real obstruction.','Need radical solvability of a non-globally-rigid three-connected generic framework, or the converse theorem in all graphs. Nongeneric rational-coordinate examples do not certify generic radical solvability.','Source Conjecture 9.4/planarity context and associated recursion inspected; no Galois computation.'),
323797:('held_signed_cancellation_gap','All block identities and W symmetry are required. Signed GMT straightening generates extra terms; reflection alone does not preserve the needed ordered boundary. Journal Conjecture 2 retains the assertion. See ORDINARY-ATTEMPTS.md.','Uniform sign-preserving/ sign-reversing boundary straightening and W reflection proof remain missing. No finite n checks prove the endpoint.','Source sole arXiv version plus journal final conjectures and signed local definitions inspected; later dissertation full body unread.'),
323802:('held_rationality_degree_gap','Fixed k=4,5,6 displayed source examples are excluded. Finite refined-ASM expansions might prove rationality, but no uniform expansion or leading-term argument was found. See ORDINARY-ATTEMPTS.md.','Need all-n rational identity for every k and degree difference exactly k-3, including possible leading cancellation. Finite interpolation is not a proof.','Source Conjecture 9 and examples read; journal points additional conjectures back to longer text. Later full dissertation not read.'),
323881:('excluded_known_resolution_and_printed_typo','Corteel-Kim-Meszaros 1704.02701 proves both volume conjectures and explicitly calls the extra factor 2 in the old C formula a typo. Literal MathDB exponent (n-1)^2+n has that extra factor; D is already proved by Kim/Zeilberger in 2014.','No new credit for the factor-of-two correction or reproducing known constant-term proofs.','Original volume formulas; 1704.02701 Conjectures 1.2/1.3 and correction paragraph; 1407.3467 actual proof section read.'),
323936:('excluded_known_shnol_theorem','Beckus-Pinchover 1706.04869 Theorem 1.1 applies with H=P,W=0 and u=phi_lambda/C. Its proof uses the ground-state unitary transform and Weyl criterion. This is known public resolution under the intended nonzero generalized-eigenfunction hypotheses.','Literal zero solution omission, if exploited, is only a wording correction and excluded. No new credit from this theorem.','All five original versions fetched; source conjecture context and later Theorem 1.1/full final proof read. Full five-version theorem-by-theorem audit not claimed.'),
323940:('held_positive_weight_opening_gadget_gap','A three-universal-hub completion creates a 3-connected graph and the intended HP race after H,t0, but Left can start t0 instead. Weight bias repairs break the exact winning threshold. See ORDINARY-ATTEMPTS.md.','Need a positive-weight opening gadget sound under every deviation, plus a separate cubic gadget for that clause. 2017 unrestricted PSPACE result does not solve these restrictions.','Both arXiv versions, journal complexity section, follow-up Theorems 2.2/2.7 construction discussion; full figure reconstruction remains open.'),
324169:('excluded_known_public_refutation','Denham-Pol-Schulze-Walther 2005.02673 Theorem 2.11 realizes every integer Euler characteristic. Its Example 2.12 prints a planar simple graph with class -2 modulo T, so planar duality handles the source Symanzik/Kirchhoff convention.','No new credit for the printed example, subdivisions, or reconstruction from its code.','Original conjecture and later Theorem 2.11, Examples 8.1/8.4 mechanism, planar convention and Example 2.12 read; no new graph proposed.'),
324193:('excluded_known_public_proof','Lin EJC 23(3) P3.15 (2016), Section 2, proves the exact two-sided gamma expansion via Visontai recurrence and induction; its alternate indexing interchanges the s+t and 1+st exponents but is the same basis.','No new credit for a formalization or another recurrence induction.','Original formula and Lin journal Conjecture 2, Lemmas 3-5 and induction body read.'),
324209:('conditional_exact_certificate_lead_no_witness','A rational 29x29 matrix rank<=14, diagonal1, entries and all 26-subset row sums in [-1,1] would be a complete counterexample via column span infinity norm. Uniform two-valued row-vertex templates are always nonsingular; source rounding clears dimensions8..13. See CANDIDATE.md.','No feasible matrix known; existence or full rank>=15 remains unproved. Publisher returned HTML; remaining citing bodies and current Omega subtree changes not cleared.','Both arXiv versions, accepted author manuscript, source matrix equivalence, row-polytope proof and explicit lower constructions read. Publisher content not a PDF.'),
324213:('excluded_known_forest_no_minus_theorem','Kinnersley-West-Zamani forest no-minus theorem is cited explicitly as Theorem1.3 in a later primary journal article: every partially dominated forest satisfies gamma_g<=gamma_g_prime. Trees with empty dominated set are an immediate known instance.','No new credit for a routine published-corollary bridge or finite minimax certificate.','Original two-version conjecture and known small cases read; later primary article full displayed no-minus theorem located, original Kinnersley proof body not fetched. Status exclusion is conservative, not a new proof claim.'),
324401:('parked_complexity_reduction','Source Conjecture1 asks the remaining r=2k+1 higher-power case. Girth means a restriction on an existential root, so graph-power verification and gadgets are needed. k=1 is polynomial but cannot refute NP-completeness unconditionally without separating P and NP.','Need a full parameter-uniform hardness reduction preserving required root girth. Source k=2 square-root result does not establish all powers.','Source concluding problem formulation and conjecture read; later dichotomy literature not exhausted.'),
324466:('parked_building_embedding_obstruction','Source Theorem7.1 proves large classes; Conjecture8.1 asks all finite thick buildings. Known independent atom configurations cover listed symplectic/Hermitian cases and cannot be counted again.','Need an obstruction in every remaining irreducible building and join transport; a building with explicit low-dimensional embedding would require full source classification fidelity.','Primary Theorem7.1 cases, Conjecture8.1 and outlook inspected; current action-dimension literature incomplete.'),
324469:('parked_lonely_runner_equivalence','The finite cyclic formulation has an existential n and x for every positive-velocity set S. It is the general Lonely Runner conjecture, not a fixed finite problem. A failure for one modulus is not a counterexample.','Need one S for which every modulus fails, or a full construction for arbitrary positive S. Allowing velocity0 merely exploits a natural-number convention and carries no credit.','Primary finite-group formulation inspected; famous hard topic parked without modulus sweeps.')}
